WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:06.987
<i>QUINCY [IN RUSSIAN]:</i>

2
00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:21.213
<i>MAN:
Quincy. stack them two and two?</i>

3
00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:24.855
<i>RACHEL: We'll need
another 20 amps for a new circuit...</i>

4
00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:27.471
at least three laptops.
four external hard drives.

5
00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:30.359
- You can leave that right there. Thank you.
<i>MAN: Yes. ma'am.</i>

6
00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:33.173
- [IN ENGLISH] Well?
- They're gonna get us what we need.

7
00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:37.959
If you mean to do this. we're gonna need
a much more comprehensive cooling system.

8
00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:40.591
- And I have told them as much.
- Vials. syringes.

9
00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:43.537
- We're running low on everything.
- Quincy. I know.

10
00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:46.449
We will replenish
once we get to Guantanamo Bay.

11
00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:47.752
I'm gonna ask a question.

12
00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:50.048
- And I want you to listen to me.
- Go ahead.

13
00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:52.466
You're working 20 hours a day.

14
00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:56.559
You're not sleeping.
This is a marathon. not a sprint.

15
00:00:56.560 --> 00:00:59.373
Let me go off-ship this time.

16
00:01:02.840 --> 00:01:04.421
I'll think about it.

17
00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:15.272
HUD. fire!

18
00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:20.279
Fire! Fire!

19
00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:22.488
Ready. halt. Headshot!

20
00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:25.818
Weapons on safe.

21
00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:29.305
Cossetti. keep that right arm blocked.
Make sure you lean into that recoil.

22
00:01:29.315 --> 00:01:30.820
<i>COSSETTI: Sir.</i>
- Next group!

23
00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:32.325
How are they looking?

24
00:01:32.440 --> 00:01:35.289
Janowitz has an eye.
Harris and Cossetti have the balls.

25
00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:40.039
- Depends on what we're gonna need there.
- Balls. We need the balls.

26
00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:41.488
Yes. sir.

27
00:01:41.560 --> 00:01:43.515
<i>TAG Team One advance!</i>

28
00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:47.583
TAC Two. let's go!

29
00:01:48.520 --> 00:01:49.932
Advance!

30
00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:51.658
Damn it. Miller!

31
00:01:51.760 --> 00:01:54.640
- Muzzle down!
- Sorry. sir!

32
00:01:54.660 --> 00:01:58.099
Sorry's not gonna do us any good
when you shoot his head off at Gitmo!

33
00:01:58.160 --> 00:02:01.057
Now TAC One. TAC Two. reset.
Do it again!

34
00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:07.999
- It's gonna take time. sir.
- Time is something we don't have.

35
00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:10.341
Every day we don't come home
with a vaccine...

36
00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:12.777
is a day another half a million people die.

37
00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:14.502
I want to make sure they're ready.

38
00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:17.541
- You'll get them there.
- Yes. sir.

39
00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:20.591
TAC Team One advance!

40
00:02:35.320 --> 00:02:38.724
You will operate on three-man
watch teams. 10-hour shifts.

41
00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:41.525
Captain wants a complete log
of every transmission.

42
00:02:41.560 --> 00:02:43.600
You may be hearing emergency-broadcast...

43
00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:46.143
and radio distress calls
from around the world.

44
00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:50.599
But we do not. under any circumstances.
respond or transmit.

45
00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:53.787
Strict EMCON.
Our position must remain secure.

46
00:02:53.800 --> 00:02:56.987
- So the Russians are still following us?
- We don't know that.

47
00:02:57.000 --> 00:03:00.439
Well. somebody shot a nuke
over our heads outside France.

48
00:03:00.440 --> 00:03:03.205
- You been in CIC the last five days?
- Yes. ma'am.

49
00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:07.058
<i>ALISHA: Were there any surface
or subsurface contacts?</i>

50
00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:09.543
- No. ma'am.
- Then let's not start spreading rumors.

51
00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:11.808
They can be as contagious as the virus.

52
00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:15.719
This room will be restricted access.
Comms specialists only. Got it?

53
00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:17.035
Yes. ma'am.

54
00:03:18.160 --> 00:03:20.164
Chief engineer? Give me a status.

55
00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:24.159
Sir. The fuel from the cruise ship
is absolutely filthy and just keeps degrading.

56
00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:28.239
If we don't hit pay dirt at Gitmo.
we might as well break out the oars.

57
00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:31.560
Don't wanna burn through our nozzles.
Take a couple engines off-line.

58
00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:35.079
No can do. sir. CO's ordered flank speed
all the way to Gitmo.

59
00:03:35.080 --> 00:03:38.520
- He's up to date on the condition of the fuel?
- He is. sir.

60
00:03:41.240 --> 00:03:43.244
<i>DANNY:
Here you go. boy.</i>

61
00:03:51.640 --> 00:03:55.319
- How's training going?
- I don't know exactly what we're training for.

62
00:03:55.320 --> 00:03:58.047
Just gonna find a bunch of corpses.

63
00:04:01.960 --> 00:04:04.084
It must be tough...

64
00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:06.701
having to train someone
to replace Frankie.

65
00:04:11.360 --> 00:04:13.026
I'm getting sick of this grub.

66
00:04:13.080 --> 00:04:17.119
I hope we find something other than
mashed potatoes and cling peaches in Cuba.

67
00:04:17.120 --> 00:04:18.701
[DANNY WHISTLES & DOG WOOFS]

68
00:04:18.760 --> 00:04:21.271
- Danny.
- What?

69
00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:22.639
You're not dealing.

70
00:04:23.520 --> 00:04:25.222
Frankie's dead.

71
00:04:25.320 --> 00:04:27.661
So are my parents. probably.
and so are yours...

72
00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:30.057
and everyone else's
in the whole damn world.

73
00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:33.053
So. what exactly is the proper way
for me to be dealing?

74
00:04:41.640 --> 00:04:44.235
<i>MAN [OVER RADIO]:
We're low on food.</i>

75
00:04:44.280 --> 00:04:47.684
<i>Low on water. We need help.</i>

76
00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:50.231
<i>We're in a warehouse off of Route 17.</i>

77
00:04:51.120 --> 00:04:52.954
<i>I'm with my two boys. so...</i>

78
00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:54.995
<i>WOMAN [OVER RADIO]:
If you can hear my voice...</i>

79
00:04:55.040 --> 00:04:58.988
<i>we need medical assistance. please.
We are right at the...</i>

80
00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:03.319
<i>MILLER: I don't really feel comfortable
speaking in public...</i>

81
00:05:03.320 --> 00:05:07.315
but I just wanted to say something
about my mother...

82
00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:09.154
who's in Iowa somewhere. I hope.

83
00:05:11.400 --> 00:05:13.911
God. please look over her and keep her safe.

84
00:05:14.840 --> 00:05:16.421
<i>JETER:
What's her name. son?</i>

85
00:05:16.520 --> 00:05:19.924
Barbara.
Barbara Miller.

86
00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:22.107
This is her.

87
00:05:28.760 --> 00:05:31.777
I'd like to say a prayer for my boyfriend.

88
00:05:32.200 --> 00:05:34.204
His name's Mickey.

89
00:05:34.280 --> 00:05:37.045
Well. his real name's Morris.

90
00:05:37.080 --> 00:05:38.914
I...

91
00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:42.320
He hates having his picture taken...

92
00:05:42.360 --> 00:05:44.484
so I've just got this one.

93
00:05:45.640 --> 00:05:48.151
It's a selfie.

94
00:05:48.760 --> 00:05:50.959
<i>O'CONNOR:
This is my father. Paul.</i>

95
00:05:50.960 --> 00:05:53.324
My brothers. Nate and Ronnie.

96
00:05:53.440 --> 00:05:56.439
Couldn't get through to them.
so I don't know where they are.

97
00:05:56.440 --> 00:05:58.781
Like most of us. I guess.

98
00:06:00.200 --> 00:06:03.894
But. um. what keeps me going...

99
00:06:03.920 --> 00:06:07.107
is the idea that we might
be able to help them somehow.

100
00:06:07.560 --> 00:06:11.894
You know. maybe there is a reason
we were out there in the Arctic all that time.

101
00:06:12.200 --> 00:06:14.072
Maybe this is God's plan for us.

102
00:06:15.320 --> 00:06:16.901
Amen to that.

103
00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:18.365
<i>ALL:
Amen.</i>

104
00:06:19.360 --> 00:06:21.568
<i>RACHEL:
The rules of the virus are these.</i>

105
00:06:22.040 --> 00:06:25.239
It's airborne. You can get it
from anyone who's a carrier...

106
00:06:25.240 --> 00:06:28.959
anyone manifesting the disease.
even a recently deceased corpse.

107
00:06:28.960 --> 00:06:31.893
Typical symptoms are lethargy
and a cough...

108
00:06:31.920 --> 00:06:34.769
followed by bleeding sores
and hemorrhaging...

109
00:06:34.800 --> 00:06:37.479
ending in dementia and total blood loss.

110
00:06:37.480 --> 00:06:40.329
- How long is the incubation period?
<i>RACHEL: Three to five days.</i>

111
00:06:40.720 --> 00:06:44.519
At least. that's what I understood
from my last contact with the CDC.

112
00:06:44.520 --> 00:06:46.222
And when was that?

113
00:06:46.320 --> 00:06:48.444
Three weeks ago
when we were in the Arctic.

114
00:06:49.160 --> 00:06:51.840
Are you saying the incubation period
can change?

115
00:06:51.880 --> 00:06:54.052
The virus has been mutating for some time...

116
00:06:54.080 --> 00:06:57.359
although I believe now
that it's been altered. it's stabilized.

117
00:06:57.360 --> 00:06:58.857
You believe?

118
00:07:01.800 --> 00:07:02.946
What about animals?

119
00:07:04.280 --> 00:07:07.719
If you're concerned about Halsey.
dogs happen to be immune.

120
00:07:07.720 --> 00:07:10.959
Animals can contract the disease.
They can't transmit it to humans.

121
00:07:10.960 --> 00:07:14.879
- I thought the birds were the original carriers.
<i>RACHEL: The birds were the carriers.</i>

122
00:07:14.880 --> 00:07:17.343
The virus jumped.
probably from their feces...

123
00:07:17.400 --> 00:07:19.911
to a mammal before mutating
and landing on us.

124
00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:23.199
After several mutations.
it was artificially altered.

125
00:07:23.200 --> 00:07:25.880
It is that version of the mutated strain...

126
00:07:25.920 --> 00:07:29.399
that is currently devastating our planet.

127
00:07:29.400 --> 00:07:33.679
So CBR gear at all times.
except outside in open spaces.

128
00:07:33.680 --> 00:07:37.199
- Masks can be off to preserve your oxygen.
- And inside?

129
00:07:37.200 --> 00:07:40.097
<i>RACHEL: One infected person
could jeopardize this entire ship...</i>

130
00:07:40.680 --> 00:07:42.599
simply by breathing.

131
00:07:46.760 --> 00:07:50.719
Question. Before we send our men
into a hot zone...

132
00:07:50.720 --> 00:07:52.471
if the virus keeps mutating...

133
00:07:52.520 --> 00:07:55.519
and you haven't heard from homeland
in almost a month...

134
00:07:55.520 --> 00:07:57.814
how can you be sure
of what you're sure of?

135
00:08:04.480 --> 00:08:08.644
If I had any doubt about what I was saying...

136
00:08:09.920 --> 00:08:11.285
I would tell you.

137
00:08:12.840 --> 00:08:14.288
I would hope so.

138
00:08:15.800 --> 00:08:18.649
I see you've cooled off.

139
00:08:18.840 --> 00:08:22.027
- I'm fine.
- Then what was that?

140
00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:25.533
Just asking questions.

141
00:08:25.600 --> 00:08:29.040
You were undermining her
in front of the officers.

142
00:08:32.600 --> 00:08:34.640
I know. Mike.

143
00:08:34.720 --> 00:08:37.097
She lied to us for four months.

144
00:08:37.200 --> 00:08:39.458
While she was talking to home every week...

145
00:08:39.520 --> 00:08:42.369
we didn't even get a chance
to warn our families.

146
00:08:42.400 --> 00:08:45.466
- We're just supposed to get over that?
- Yeah. we are.

147
00:08:46.720 --> 00:08:49.351
She's got a long way to go
before she earns my trust.

148
00:08:49.360 --> 00:08:51.279
- That's all.
- What about me?

149
00:08:53.040 --> 00:08:57.039
There's no Navy. no infrastructure.
no food or fuel supply.

150
00:08:57.040 --> 00:09:02.319
We don't know what we're gonna find. and
we're gonna have to improvise every step.

151
00:09:02.320 --> 00:09:04.783
- Now. I'm gonna need my XO...
- To fall in line?

152
00:09:06.200 --> 00:09:08.408
To execute.

153
00:09:09.520 --> 00:09:12.919
Whether or not he agrees with my decisions.

154
00:09:12.920 --> 00:09:15.919
Now. I'm gonna ask you one time
and one time only:

155
00:09:15.920 --> 00:09:17.586
Are you with me?

156
00:09:18.640 --> 00:09:21.405
I took an oath.
and I still respect the chain of command.

157
00:09:21.440 --> 00:09:24.506
- That wasn't my question.
- I'm with you.

158
00:09:31.160 --> 00:09:33.032
You really think she can do this?

159
00:09:34.240 --> 00:09:36.617
She's the only hope we got.

160
00:10:04.320 --> 00:10:06.154
<i>PILOT:
Coming over Gitmo now.</i>

161
00:10:06.200 --> 00:10:08.927
Negative visual contact.

162
00:10:09.960 --> 00:10:12.254
<i>Negative movement.</i>

163
00:10:12.280 --> 00:10:13.596
<i>DANNY:
Where is everybody?</i>

164
00:10:14.680 --> 00:10:17.191
<i>PILOT:
Same on thermals.</i>

165
00:10:19.000 --> 00:10:21.294
<i>We have zero. copy.
zero ground movement.</i>

166
00:10:21.320 --> 00:10:24.319
There were 9000 people stationed there.

167
00:10:24.880 --> 00:10:28.791
Food warehouse and hospital look
spread out. Fuel rig's all the way up there.

168
00:10:30.200 --> 00:10:32.408
That's why we're gonna go with three teams.

169
00:10:32.520 --> 00:10:34.861
I'll take the warehouse.
You'll hit the hospital.

170
00:10:34.920 --> 00:10:37.467
- Fuel team ready?
- We are. sir.

171
00:10:37.520 --> 00:10:40.754
Stay frosty. Something about this
doesn't feel right.

172
00:10:40.800 --> 00:10:42.466
Yes. sir.

173
00:10:48.720 --> 00:10:51.479
You're absolutely the most
obstinate person I've met.

174
00:10:51.480 --> 00:10:54.159
- You know that?
- I don't know everyone you've met.

175
00:10:54.160 --> 00:10:57.199
- It's insane.
- If I let you go. you'll be out there all week.

176
00:10:57.200 --> 00:10:59.711
- You're too meticulous.
- What if something happens?

177
00:10:59.760 --> 00:11:01.800
He's right. We can't risk you leaving.

178
00:11:02.240 --> 00:11:04.879
- Thank you. I'll get my suit.
<i>CHANDLER: Not so fast. Dr. Tophet.</i>

179
00:11:04.880 --> 00:11:07.307
- We can't risk either of you.
<i>QUINCY: That's flattering...</i>

180
00:11:07.320 --> 00:11:09.831
How do you plan on getting us the supplies?

181
00:11:09.880 --> 00:11:12.174
Not to underestimate
your men's capabilities...

182
00:11:12.200 --> 00:11:15.351
but it's highly unlikely
they're gonna identify what we need.

183
00:11:15.360 --> 00:11:18.919
If we can knock an ICBM out of the sky.
I think we can handle this.

184
00:11:18.920 --> 00:11:22.022
An officer will escort you both to CIC.

185
00:11:22.040 --> 00:11:23.573
And what about you. captain?

186
00:11:26.560 --> 00:11:28.311
What if something happens to you?

187
00:11:28.760 --> 00:11:30.547
The mission will go on...

188
00:11:30.600 --> 00:11:33.439
in Commander Slattery's
very capable hands.

189
00:11:33.440 --> 00:11:36.253
After last night's performance.
I'm not so sure.

190
00:11:36.280 --> 00:11:41.084
Well. we're all out on a limb here. aren't we?

191
00:12:00.920 --> 00:12:04.445
Vulture Team is feet dry on the east beach.
Proceed to first objective.

192
00:12:27.840 --> 00:12:30.098
Approaching the south gate.

193
00:12:38.000 --> 00:12:39.955
Cobra Team is approaching the hospital.

194
00:12:51.200 --> 00:12:52.432
Over here.

195
00:12:59.080 --> 00:13:01.338
We've attached a helmet cam
to Lieutenant Green.

196
00:13:01.440 --> 00:13:04.439
We can see everything he does
and communicate to him by UHF.

197
00:13:04.440 --> 00:13:05.805
So you can get what you need.

198
00:13:08.120 --> 00:13:10.414
It'll be fine.

199
00:13:10.440 --> 00:13:11.973
That's my chair.

200
00:13:17.320 --> 00:13:20.217
I understand people aren't
particularly thrilled with me...

201
00:13:21.200 --> 00:13:23.155
but I had orders.

202
00:13:23.200 --> 00:13:24.781
From the Pentagon.

203
00:13:25.560 --> 00:13:26.875
<i>KARA:
We understand orders.</i>

204
00:13:27.680 --> 00:13:30.107
We follow them every day.

205
00:13:35.240 --> 00:13:36.652
Masks on.

206
00:13:36.720 --> 00:13:39.400
- Masks on.
<i>CRUZ: All right. masks up.</i>

207
00:13:39.480 --> 00:13:42.750
We've got 60 minutes of air at max conserve.

208
00:13:45.080 --> 00:13:48.164
Chief Lynn. XO.
<i>Fuel team's approaching the rigs.</i>

209
00:13:48.165 --> 00:13:51.388
- Expect to receive fuel within 15 minutes.
<i>LYNN [OVER RADIO]: Roger. XO.</i>

210
00:14:00.760 --> 00:14:03.137
We need to find the valve wheel.

211
00:14:03.200 --> 00:14:04.984
It couldn't have gone far.

212
00:14:04.985 --> 00:14:08.727
<i>CHANDLER [OVER RADIO]: The Vulture Team
heading due south sector. All's quiet.</i>

213
00:14:20.760 --> 00:14:21.992
[METAL CLANGS]

214
00:14:29.760 --> 00:14:32.919
Well. you bucking for a Silver Star.
aren't you. Miller?

215
00:14:32.920 --> 00:14:34.707
You can't teach courage like that.

216
00:14:34.760 --> 00:14:38.116
Follow our lead.
We'll be in and out in less than an hour.

217
00:14:41.720 --> 00:14:44.569
- Was it too much?
- Just enough.

218
00:15:02.000 --> 00:15:05.017
<i>RIOS:
Don't touch that.</i>

219
00:15:05.600 --> 00:15:09.479
You discharge that you'll flood the whole
engineering room with poisonous Halon gas.

220
00:15:09.480 --> 00:15:12.959
Uh. my state room is freezing.
and I was told these levers...

221
00:15:12.960 --> 00:15:14.794
might shut off the AC to my space.

222
00:15:15.280 --> 00:15:20.036
- By who?
- I don't know. One of the enlisted men.

223
00:15:22.000 --> 00:15:24.341
Do us a favor.
Don't touch anything on the ship.

224
00:15:24.440 --> 00:15:26.480
- Of course.
- If you need help. ask for it.

225
00:15:26.520 --> 00:15:28.983
- Very sorry.
- Okay.

226
00:16:06.040 --> 00:16:07.912
[GAGS]

227
00:16:10.160 --> 00:16:13.480
Eyes in front of you.
And do not puke in your mask.

228
00:16:14.360 --> 00:16:17.764
<i>KARA:
Is that what it was like on the cruise ship?</i>

229
00:16:18.400 --> 00:16:20.863
None of them wanna talk about it.

230
00:16:22.280 --> 00:16:24.827
That's because there are no words.

231
00:16:40.320 --> 00:16:42.915
Nathan James. Tiger Team. we're all set.

232
00:16:42.920 --> 00:16:45.515
<i>SLATTERY [OVER RADIO]:
Copy that. We are ready to receive.</i>

233
00:16:45.560 --> 00:16:49.239
CCS Bridge. your martini is on its way.

234
00:16:49.240 --> 00:16:51.751
One. two. three.

235
00:16:57.080 --> 00:17:01.668
One more time. We got it. One. two. three.

236
00:17:03.600 --> 00:17:05.724
[HUMMING]

237
00:17:10.360 --> 00:17:13.125
Bridge. CCS. fueling commenced.

238
00:17:16.440 --> 00:17:18.444
- We're in.
- You're looking for steroids.

239
00:17:18.520 --> 00:17:20.778
Interferon. Ribavirin.

240
00:17:20.800 --> 00:17:23.849
<i>Any broad-spectrum antibiotics
you can find.</i>

241
00:17:23.850 --> 00:17:27.459
<i>We need plastic ware.
monitoring equipment. culture plates.</i>

242
00:17:27.720 --> 00:17:29.035
Show me the whole room.

243
00:17:30.440 --> 00:17:32.612
Bring it round slowly.

244
00:17:33.720 --> 00:17:35.422
Over to the right.

245
00:17:35.480 --> 00:17:37.231
Back. back. back! Back to the left.

246
00:17:40.040 --> 00:17:41.706
Move forward. Closer.

247
00:17:43.840 --> 00:17:47.263
- That's it. That's a centrifuge.
<i>DANNY [OVER RADIO]: Got it.</i>

248
00:17:51.640 --> 00:17:53.934
<i>CHANDLER:
No apparent activity in Sector Charlie 5.</i>

249
00:17:54.000 --> 00:17:56.539
<i>Vulture Team proceeding directly to objective.</i>

250
00:17:56.540 --> 00:17:57.952
Copy that. Vulture One.

251
00:18:20.520 --> 00:18:21.666
Masks.

252
00:18:26.920 --> 00:18:29.515
<i>TEX:
I'm an American! Get the hell out of there!</i>

253
00:18:29.520 --> 00:18:32.200
Don't! Get out! Stop it!

254
00:18:32.280 --> 00:18:33.982
Get the hell out of there!

255
00:18:47.280 --> 00:18:50.853
<i>MAN 1:
Burk! Get up. get up. get going! Weapons.</i>

256
00:18:52.880 --> 00:18:55.004
[MAN 2 SHOUTING INDISTINCTLY]

257
00:18:55.840 --> 00:18:59.233
<i>I'm American. I'm friendly.</i>

258
00:19:00.040 --> 00:19:02.239
- I'm a friendly American.
- This is Vulture.

259
00:19:02.240 --> 00:19:05.919
We're under attack
by unknown number of hostiles.

260
00:19:05.920 --> 00:19:07.235
Stand by for fire mission.

261
00:19:07.320 --> 00:19:10.760
Set General Quarters!
Threat warning red. weapons tight!

262
00:19:11.160 --> 00:19:14.639
General Quarters. General Quarters.
All hands. man your battle stations.

263
00:19:14.640 --> 00:19:18.165
Light off mount five one.
Shift to local ready surface.

264
00:19:19.760 --> 00:19:22.137
Vulture One. Nathan James.
do we have a target?

265
00:19:22.200 --> 00:19:26.079
Negative. Cobra Team.
Tiger Team. be advised.

266
00:19:26.080 --> 00:19:27.999
Hostiles operating on base.

267
00:19:28.000 --> 00:19:30.669
<i>IEDs are being employed. Set fipcom delta.</i>

268
00:19:30.680 --> 00:19:31.912
<i>WOMAN:
Copy that. Vulture One.</i>

269
00:19:32.000 --> 00:19:35.066
- Master Chief. we need guns up.
- I'm on it. O'Connor.

270
00:19:35.080 --> 00:19:39.039
This is Cobra Team. We're a half mile
south-southeast from your port ops.

271
00:19:39.040 --> 00:19:41.212
<i>Say the word and we will provide backup.</i>

272
00:19:41.280 --> 00:19:44.684
Negative. I don't want you walking
into an ambush. Stay on mission.

273
00:19:45.440 --> 00:19:47.395
Yes. sir.

274
00:19:48.240 --> 00:19:51.342
- Back up!
- Jesus. guys. I'm on your side!

275
00:19:51.360 --> 00:19:53.279
I said. back up!

276
00:19:53.360 --> 00:19:54.772
I'm not sick.

277
00:19:54.920 --> 00:19:59.555
Even the ass-bags
who tried to kill you are not sick!

278
00:20:01.400 --> 00:20:04.127
All right. set cover. But let him come.

279
00:20:04.160 --> 00:20:07.311
<i>BURK:
All right. step forward! Slowly!</i>

280
00:20:07.600 --> 00:20:10.147
Hey. hey. hey. keep it slow.

281
00:20:10.600 --> 00:20:15.404
Moving slow. Everybody just take it easy.

282
00:20:16.750 --> 00:20:18.247
That's far enough.

283
00:20:20.150 --> 00:20:23.506
Okay. commodore.
You wanna get the lowdown or not?

284
00:20:23.510 --> 00:20:25.212
Let's start with the ass-bags.

285
00:20:25.590 --> 00:20:29.829
- They're al Qaeda. What's left of them.
- How many?

286
00:20:29.830 --> 00:20:33.789
Fourteen altogether. but they're spread out
now to make you a welcoming party.

287
00:20:33.790 --> 00:20:36.253
- Nobody's sick?
- We were all in Section 7...

288
00:20:36.270 --> 00:20:38.997
an isolated part of the camp
for high-level detainees.

289
00:20:39.030 --> 00:20:41.407
We had our own food stocks. own facilities.

290
00:20:41.470 --> 00:20:44.826
None of us came in contact with the virus.

291
00:20:44.830 --> 00:20:46.954
Everybody else was evacuated.

292
00:20:47.030 --> 00:20:48.696
We had the run of the place.

293
00:20:48.790 --> 00:20:50.492
We?

294
00:20:50.590 --> 00:20:52.594
Me and six other guards.

295
00:20:53.350 --> 00:20:56.115
Subcontractors. private security.

296
00:20:56.550 --> 00:20:58.638
At that point. we figured...

297
00:20:58.710 --> 00:21:01.523
no governments. no politics.

298
00:21:02.350 --> 00:21:05.199
- We let them go.
- And they turned on you.

299
00:21:05.950 --> 00:21:08.038
<i>TEX:
That's what's left of my best friend.</i>

300
00:21:08.110 --> 00:21:09.776
Other guy's MIA.

301
00:21:10.710 --> 00:21:13.709
- I'm the last man standing.
- So where the hell are they?

302
00:21:13.710 --> 00:21:15.665
<i>TEX:
Most went to guard the food warehouse...</i>

303
00:21:15.750 --> 00:21:18.937
but three peeled off towards your ship
with rocket launchers.

304
00:21:18.990 --> 00:21:22.269
- You're telling me this now?
- You're the one asking the questions.

305
00:21:22.270 --> 00:21:27.069
Nathan James. Vulture One. be advised.
hostiles are armed with RPGs...

306
00:21:27.070 --> 00:21:28.603
en route to your whiskey.

307
00:21:28.710 --> 00:21:31.137
Tiger One. Nathan James. cease pumping.

308
00:21:31.190 --> 00:21:34.546
- Shut it down now.
- Secure fueling.

309
00:21:34.590 --> 00:21:37.860
So. what can you tell me
about this food warehouse?

310
00:21:37.870 --> 00:21:40.887
How to get in. but it's gonna mean
getting your hands dirty.

311
00:21:40.910 --> 00:21:42.275
I've dirtied them before.

312
00:21:43.030 --> 00:21:46.829
Tom Chandler.
CO. Nathan James. U.S. Navy.

313
00:21:46.830 --> 00:21:49.124
Tex Nolan. Welcome to Gitmo.

314
00:22:00.550 --> 00:22:02.505
Man. only got 15 PSI.

315
00:22:02.590 --> 00:22:05.017
Shit. I'm at 9 percent.

316
00:22:05.070 --> 00:22:08.426
All right. guys. listen to me.
We got a job to do here...

317
00:22:08.430 --> 00:22:10.941
<i>and we're not finished yet.</i>

318
00:22:10.950 --> 00:22:13.327
<i>No supplies. no vaccine.</i>

319
00:22:13.390 --> 00:22:16.789
No vaccine. no going home.
no seeing your families.

320
00:22:16.790 --> 00:22:19.869
- Lieutenant Green. don't take any chances.
<i>DANNY: Follow my lead.</i>

321
00:22:19.870 --> 00:22:22.550
<i>We'll be out of here in less than 10. got it?</i>

322
00:22:22.590 --> 00:22:24.714
Let's do this thing.

323
00:22:24.790 --> 00:22:26.998
Did he hear me?

324
00:22:27.990 --> 00:22:30.501
He heard you.

325
00:22:33.450 --> 00:22:35.847
<i>LYNN:
Bridge. CCS. We're still taking on fuel.</i>

326
00:22:35.910 --> 00:22:37.998
Tiger Team. what the hell's going on there?

327
00:22:38.070 --> 00:22:40.570
<i>BARNETT: The valve is frozen.
We're working on it. sir!</i>

328
00:22:40.910 --> 00:22:43.675
Come on. Ma'am. stand back.

329
00:22:44.150 --> 00:22:47.589
XO. recommend disengaging
the fuel hose on our end.

330
00:22:47.590 --> 00:22:50.389
Spill oil into the harbor
while they have RPGs? Hell. no.

331
00:22:50.390 --> 00:22:54.518
TAO. Bridge. We have hostiles incoming.
Find me a target.

332
00:22:56.110 --> 00:22:59.091
Again. One. two...

333
00:23:02.670 --> 00:23:06.327
Nathan James. the valve stem is shot. sir.
We cannot stop the fuel.

334
00:23:06.350 --> 00:23:07.931
Incoming!

335
00:23:09.590 --> 00:23:12.607
[GARNETT GROANING]

336
00:23:13.470 --> 00:23:14.665
<i>CHUNG:
Ma'am!</i>

337
00:23:17.750 --> 00:23:19.115
[GUNFIRE]

338
00:23:20.030 --> 00:23:22.569
Nathan James. this is MPA.
Chief engineer's been hit.

339
00:23:22.570 --> 00:23:24.389
<i>We need the doc up here. ASAP!</i>

340
00:23:24.390 --> 00:23:27.269
TAO. give me a targeting solution
on that terminal.

341
00:23:27.270 --> 00:23:30.674
- Aye. sir.
- OS-1. range and bearing to the terminal?

342
00:23:30.710 --> 00:23:34.066
Rough bearing two-two-zero.
approximately 1500 yards.

343
00:23:35.430 --> 00:23:38.447
They're going for the fuel tank.
They're gonna blow the ship!

344
00:23:38.470 --> 00:23:40.764
CIC. Bridge. Where's my target acquisition?

345
00:23:40.830 --> 00:23:43.763
- Slew left 30.
- Roger. left 30 degrees.

346
00:23:45.750 --> 00:23:47.922
Bridge. surface target acquired.

347
00:23:48.750 --> 00:23:50.537
Fire.

348
00:24:04.150 --> 00:24:08.829
Tiger Team. Nathan James.
<i>Doc Rios is en route. ETA five minutes.</i>

349
00:24:08.830 --> 00:24:11.207
Vulture. Cobra. Nathan James.

350
00:24:11.230 --> 00:24:14.829
All known hostiles neutralized
in the vicinity of the fuel pier.

351
00:24:14.830 --> 00:24:17.341
<i>CHANDLER:
Vulture Team. copy that.</i>

352
00:24:24.750 --> 00:24:26.386
<i>CHANDLER:
So where are they gonna be?</i>

353
00:24:26.390 --> 00:24:29.789
Oatmeal and baked beans.
It's the new women and children.

354
00:24:29.790 --> 00:24:33.635
They're holed up in that warehouse.
They're gonna make us come and get them.

355
00:24:35.590 --> 00:24:37.256
Captain.

356
00:24:42.510 --> 00:24:44.634
Animals.

357
00:24:45.910 --> 00:24:48.891
Revenge is best served cold.

358
00:24:50.870 --> 00:24:52.704
Let's eat.

359
00:24:57.590 --> 00:25:02.261
Lieutenant Green. you have everything I need.
Please get out of there now.

360
00:25:02.590 --> 00:25:05.860
Cobra One. copy. Proceeding to extract.

361
00:25:15.150 --> 00:25:16.345
[BARKS]

362
00:25:33.910 --> 00:25:35.491
[GUNFIRE]

363
00:25:38.390 --> 00:25:39.636
<i>DANNY:
Go. go! Come on!</i>

364
00:25:41.190 --> 00:25:42.771
Go!

365
00:25:43.550 --> 00:25:46.870
Sir. Cobra Team's trapped inside the hospital.
running out of air.

366
00:25:56.670 --> 00:25:59.629
We located the shooters outside the hospital?
Have a target?

367
00:25:59.630 --> 00:26:01.670
<i>BARKER: Negative. sir.</i>
- Patch me in to Green.

368
00:26:01.750 --> 00:26:03.501
- I'm out of air!
- Two percent.

369
00:26:03.590 --> 00:26:06.523
- Almost nothing.
- Couple of minutes. max!

370
00:26:06.550 --> 00:26:09.349
I'm gonna peel off Vulture
to give you reinforcements.

371
00:26:09.350 --> 00:26:14.154
Negative. They're too far away. They will
never get here in time. But I got an idea.

372
00:26:15.150 --> 00:26:18.928
Copy that. Vulture Team preparing
to hit the warehouse. Lead the way.

373
00:27:08.430 --> 00:27:10.048
Where are they?

374
00:27:15.150 --> 00:27:17.491
[GUNFIRE]

375
00:27:34.030 --> 00:27:35.817
Grenade!

376
00:27:55.790 --> 00:27:58.895
<i>DANNY: Cruz. what's your status?
CRUZ: On the stairs approaching the roof.</i>

377
00:27:58.900 --> 00:28:01.072
- Ten seconds out.
<i>DANNY: Check.</i>

378
00:28:14.910 --> 00:28:16.661
We got this. boy.

379
00:28:16.790 --> 00:28:19.385
<i>No worries.</i>

380
00:28:21.790 --> 00:28:23.962
<i>Troops are on the ropes.</i>

381
00:28:24.550 --> 00:28:25.782
<i>Extracting now.</i>

382
00:28:31.670 --> 00:28:33.794
[ALARM BEEPING]

383
00:28:36.070 --> 00:28:38.919
<i>CRUZ:
We're in position. Stand by to engage.</i>

384
00:28:47.350 --> 00:28:48.847
[GUNFIRE]

385
00:28:51.270 --> 00:28:52.767
[GROANS]

386
00:28:53.830 --> 00:28:56.002
[GASPING]

387
00:29:08.310 --> 00:29:09.758
[GUNSHOT]

388
00:29:09.770 --> 00:29:11.642
<i>DANNY:
He's hit! Man down! Man down!</i>

389
00:29:13.830 --> 00:29:15.581
Damn it! We need the doc out here!

390
00:29:15.670 --> 00:29:18.181
Sir. he's with Tiger One
by the fueling station.

391
00:29:18.230 --> 00:29:20.402
Commander...

392
00:29:20.470 --> 00:29:23.657
I worked a year in a trauma ward
in Mogadishu.

393
00:29:26.550 --> 00:29:28.131
Gear up.

394
00:29:29.790 --> 00:29:31.408
[GUNFIRE]

395
00:29:42.630 --> 00:29:44.888
[BOTH GRUNTING]

396
00:29:57.990 --> 00:29:59.608
[GROANS]

397
00:30:00.750 --> 00:30:03.683
Stay with me. Cruz. Just stay with me.

398
00:30:06.390 --> 00:30:10.909
Get him stabilized. then get off the beach.
First whiff of hostilities. you are out. Got it?

399
00:30:10.910 --> 00:30:13.675
I read you loud and clear. commander.

400
00:30:14.270 --> 00:30:17.589
TAO. I want five-inch CIWS in surface mode
focused on that beach.

401
00:30:17.590 --> 00:30:19.123
Aye. sir.

402
00:30:19.670 --> 00:30:21.811
<i>RACHEL: What have we got?</i>
- What? Where's the doc?

403
00:30:21.830 --> 00:30:24.805
He's up at the fueling tank.
Your chief engineer was injured as well.

404
00:30:24.810 --> 00:30:27.237
- Lay him down.
- Get him down.

405
00:30:28.990 --> 00:30:30.784
<i>DANNY: Here you go.</i>
- You. hold that.

406
00:30:30.810 --> 00:30:32.428
<i>DANNY: Set up a perimeter.</i>
- All right.

407
00:30:32.990 --> 00:30:34.523
<i>SMITH: Yes. sir.</i>

408
00:30:36.970 --> 00:30:39.142
<i>COSSETTI: Get over watch.
DANNY: Come on.</i>

409
00:30:39.248 --> 00:30:41.648
<i>SMITH: Got the high point.
DANNY: He's gonna bleed out. Wait!</i>

410
00:30:41.650 --> 00:30:43.870
- Somebody get doc!
<i>RACHEL: We don't have time to wait.</i>

411
00:30:43.875 --> 00:30:47.374
There's nothing a medic can do
that we cannot. If you want to help...

412
00:30:47.430 --> 00:30:50.195
hold him still and listen
to every word that I say.

413
00:30:51.670 --> 00:30:54.857
Come on. Stay with me. Look at me.
You're gonna be all right.

414
00:30:57.230 --> 00:30:58.595
[GRUNTS]

415
00:31:00.110 --> 00:31:02.318
<i>DANNY: Let's go. come on.
Blood pressure's dropping.</i>

416
00:31:03.950 --> 00:31:05.869
Hold that!

417
00:31:07.150 --> 00:31:10.167
Going back in. Okay.

418
00:31:10.190 --> 00:31:12.362
Hey. Come on. stay with me.
Look at me. Stay with me.

419
00:31:14.710 --> 00:31:18.319
If you do not close this artery. he's dead.

420
00:31:20.430 --> 00:31:22.264
Got it.

421
00:31:30.630 --> 00:31:32.332
He's stabilized.

422
00:31:49.830 --> 00:31:50.940
Hey. commodore.

423
00:31:55.190 --> 00:31:58.039
Don't give them a damn thing.

424
00:32:18.630 --> 00:32:23.386
This here is Amir. He's a big fan of IEDs
and mutilating American soldiers.

425
00:32:23.910 --> 00:32:26.675
Amir. my name is Tom Chandler. U.S. Navy.

426
00:32:27.310 --> 00:32:28.758
You don't want to do this.

427
00:32:29.550 --> 00:32:32.061
Tex is the man who let you go
from your cells.

428
00:32:32.110 --> 00:32:35.909
- He is no different from the others.
- Hey. feeling's mutual. you dirty...

429
00:32:35.910 --> 00:32:39.012
Vulture Team. Nathan James.
I need a status update.

430
00:32:42.310 --> 00:32:44.182
Vulture Team. Nathan James. Status?

431
00:32:44.230 --> 00:32:46.957
<i>CHANDLER: Nathan James. Vulture One.
We're at the food warehouse.</i>

432
00:32:47.870 --> 00:32:51.549
Just trying to deal with a little hostage
situation over here.

433
00:32:51.550 --> 00:32:54.669
<i>AMIR [OVER RADIO]: Who are you talking to?
CHANDLER: I'm answering my ship's call.</i>

434
00:32:54.670 --> 00:32:58.469
Otherwise. they'll panic.
start shelling the whole place.

435
00:32:58.470 --> 00:33:01.017
- He wants a diversion.
<i>CHANDLER: All we 're doing is talking.</i>

436
00:33:01.110 --> 00:33:05.021
<i>- Let's not get anybody else killed here.
AMIR: No more talking to them. Talk to me!</i>

437
00:33:05.030 --> 00:33:09.109
Prepare the five-inch. Focus fire on
Building 35. Stand by for exact coordinates.

438
00:33:09.110 --> 00:33:10.897
Nishioka. eyes on.

439
00:33:13.390 --> 00:33:18.989
- Leave all food on this side of the building.
- Not enough of you to eat that in 10 lifetimes.

440
00:33:18.990 --> 00:33:20.523
<i>CHANDLER:
Look.</i>

441
00:33:20.670 --> 00:33:24.429
Amir. it's a new world now.

442
00:33:24.430 --> 00:33:26.518
There's no good guys and bad guys.

443
00:33:26.590 --> 00:33:30.284
Doesn't matter which side we were on.
We're all just trying to survive.

444
00:33:30.670 --> 00:33:33.589
We don't want to hurt you any more
than you want to hurt us.

445
00:33:33.590 --> 00:33:36.487
<i>But you know I'm not leaving here
without my man.</i>

446
00:33:37.670 --> 00:33:39.964
- So when you let Tex go...
- If I let him go!

447
00:33:40.070 --> 00:33:45.149
When you let him go. we'll be on our way.

448
00:33:45.150 --> 00:33:47.358
I'll decide how much food we leave you with.

449
00:33:47.430 --> 00:33:49.638
<i>AMIR:
No! Enough of this!</i>

450
00:33:50.310 --> 00:33:52.568
Listen to me. Amir.

451
00:33:53.590 --> 00:33:56.571
<i>You want the entire southwest
corner of the warehouse.</i>

452
00:33:57.110 --> 00:33:58.861
Focus fire Building 35. southwest corner.

453
00:33:58.910 --> 00:34:03.909
That's almost half the food in the entire place.
Is that gonna make you happy?

454
00:34:03.910 --> 00:34:08.498
No. You will leave all the food
on this side of the building. or he dies.

455
00:34:09.230 --> 00:34:11.910
Well. now. see.
we got a bit of a problem with that.

456
00:34:11.950 --> 00:34:15.813
Because there's one thing from the old world
that still applies today...

457
00:34:16.310 --> 00:34:18.568
something that will never change.

458
00:34:25.190 --> 00:34:27.737
- Target acquired.
- Fire!

459
00:34:29.230 --> 00:34:31.234
We don't negotiate with terrorists.

460
00:34:49.310 --> 00:34:51.398
<i>Clear!</i>

461
00:34:51.510 --> 00:34:52.789
Nice.

462
00:34:52.870 --> 00:34:54.149
Yes.

463
00:34:54.870 --> 00:34:57.936
Good work. good work.

464
00:35:20.790 --> 00:35:23.789
I don't know how you feel about the water...

465
00:35:23.790 --> 00:35:26.048
but we sure could use your services.

466
00:35:26.110 --> 00:35:27.342
Where you headed?

467
00:35:27.510 --> 00:35:31.638
We got some things to do.
but when we're done. we're going home.

468
00:35:33.190 --> 00:35:35.024
Yeah. I'll sign up for that.

469
00:35:37.590 --> 00:35:42.189
<i>CHANDLER: Nathan James. Vulture One.
Hostage situation resolved.</i>

470
00:35:42.190 --> 00:35:44.024
Thank you for the close shave.

471
00:35:44.150 --> 00:35:46.999
We are inbound.

472
00:35:54.350 --> 00:35:57.509
<i>ALISHA [OVER PA]: Now go to your stations.
all special sea and anchor detail.</i>

473
00:35:57.510 --> 00:36:00.141
Nathan James <i>will get under way at 1700.</i>

474
00:36:00.150 --> 00:36:04.013
<i>All departments make manned and ready
special reports to the XO on the bridge.</i>

475
00:36:09.270 --> 00:36:11.021
Captain's on the bridge.

476
00:36:12.190 --> 00:36:13.977
<i>Hey-</i>

477
00:36:14.030 --> 00:36:17.669
We're loading up RHIBs and SDV subs.
Trucks are bringing over the food.

478
00:36:17.670 --> 00:36:20.869
- Suppo thinks it's gonna last five. six weeks.
- And fuel?

479
00:36:20.870 --> 00:36:24.549
We lost suction on the tank at 96 percent.

480
00:36:24.550 --> 00:36:28.069
And the chief engineer took some shrapnel.
She's gonna be okay. though.

481
00:36:28.070 --> 00:36:31.869
- Tough as nails. that one.
- When push comes to shove. they all are.

482
00:36:31.870 --> 00:36:35.509
Gentlemen. apparently one of the machines
in the lab got tipped over.

483
00:36:35.510 --> 00:36:40.069
Dr. Tophet is insists he needs time to secure
and recalibrate before we move the ship.

484
00:36:40.070 --> 00:36:43.172
- How long?
- He says three to four hours.

485
00:36:44.470 --> 00:36:45.785
Where's Dr. Scott?

486
00:36:47.350 --> 00:36:48.798
Still in medical.

487
00:36:51.750 --> 00:36:53.622
Was a tough call.

488
00:36:54.710 --> 00:36:55.820
We did good today.

489
00:36:56.990 --> 00:37:01.149
Captain. I'm picking up a contact headed
for the harbor. Negative electronic signature.

490
00:37:01.150 --> 00:37:04.709
They're not operating their radar.
Cannot make a positive ID.

491
00:37:04.710 --> 00:37:07.549
Vessel 21 miles southeast.
Guantanamo Bay...

492
00:37:07.550 --> 00:37:11.669
this is U.S. Navy warship one-five-one
hailing you on channel one-six.

493
00:37:11.670 --> 00:37:14.097
Identify yourself. over.

494
00:37:15.790 --> 00:37:18.421
<i>WOMAN [OVER RADIO]:
This is British Naval vessel HMS Suffolk...</i>

495
00:37:18.430 --> 00:37:19.340
<i>SLATTERY:
Confirm that.</i>

496
00:37:19.355 --> 00:37:23.940
<i>Hull number five-two-five. IMO call sign
whiskey-echo-bravo-two-three-six.</i>

497
00:37:23.950 --> 00:37:27.692
<i>None of us have been infected.
but we're running low on food.</i>

498
00:37:27.710 --> 00:37:30.004
<i>We've been searching
for a place to replenish...</i>

499
00:37:30.030 --> 00:37:32.202
<i>- and repair our radar.
- Confirmed. sir.</i>

500
00:37:38.470 --> 00:37:43.269
This is Commander Tom Chandler.
Commanding Officer. USS Nathan James.

501
00:37:43.270 --> 00:37:45.611
We welcome you to Guantanamo Bay.

502
00:37:45.630 --> 00:37:49.229
Wish you would've been here
a few hours ago. We could've used the help.

503
00:37:49.230 --> 00:37:52.389
<i>I assure you that next time.
we will be there for you...</i>

504
00:37:52.390 --> 00:37:54.731
<i>should you choose
to accept an association.</i>

505
00:37:54.750 --> 00:38:00.364
Well. we'll put some pot pies in the oven and
some fish and chips in the fryer. Come on in.

506
00:38:01.270 --> 00:38:05.549
We can't go anywhere till the lab's fixed.
Let's prepare to greet our new friends.

507
00:38:05.550 --> 00:38:07.674
XO has the lead.

508
00:38:09.390 --> 00:38:10.500
Ow.

509
00:38:10.630 --> 00:38:11.909
Oh. that stings.

510
00:38:12.090 --> 00:38:14.535
<i>RACHEL:
It's supposed to sting. I'm cleaning it.</i>

511
00:38:14.540 --> 00:38:16.512
- I don't need it cleaned.
- Yes. you do.

512
00:38:17.510 --> 00:38:19.212
<i>RIOS:
This is gonna sting a little.</i>

513
00:38:21.830 --> 00:38:24.257
<i>CHANDLER: How you doing. eng?</i>
- All right. sir.

514
00:38:24.350 --> 00:38:30.000
- Doc says I'll be on my feet soon enough.
- No rush. We got it all under control.

515
00:38:34.190 --> 00:38:35.336
She saved him.

516
00:38:39.470 --> 00:38:42.826
She's gonna save us all. Right. Dr. Scott?

517
00:38:42.870 --> 00:38:46.057
Well. hopefully. we'll save each other.

518
00:38:46.710 --> 00:38:48.122
Real soulful. this one.

519
00:38:48.190 --> 00:38:52.349
Never mind them good looks.
that brassy exterior.

520
00:38:52.350 --> 00:38:53.883
Word?

521
00:39:00.870 --> 00:39:03.465
I know. Don't do it again.

522
00:39:03.510 --> 00:39:05.768
You don't have anything to prove...

523
00:39:07.550 --> 00:39:09.977
if that's what it was about.

524
00:39:12.590 --> 00:39:14.509
And don't do it again.

525
00:39:18.710 --> 00:39:21.797
<i>TEX:
Hey! Nursey!</i>

526
00:39:21.910 --> 00:39:24.843
I need a cold compress here.

527
00:39:40.510 --> 00:39:42.261
Spoils of war.

528
00:40:14.950 --> 00:40:18.607
You know. I should be getting this stuff
ready for his family.

529
00:40:22.750 --> 00:40:24.705
But. uh...

530
00:40:27.030 --> 00:40:29.541
there's nobody even to give it to.

531
00:40:40.190 --> 00:40:41.892
<i>MAN 1:
Captain's on the bridge.</i>

532
00:40:41.990 --> 00:40:44.453
- They in sight?
- Yeah.

533
00:40:44.470 --> 00:40:47.487
I hear they serve Guinness on board.

534
00:40:49.310 --> 00:40:55.128
Sir. E-DUB can't confirm the signature on
that vessel. but they don't think it's British.

535
00:40:58.830 --> 00:41:00.145
<i>CHANDLER:
It's the Russians.</i>

536
00:41:00.270 --> 00:41:01.767
Set General Quarters now!

537
00:41:01.830 --> 00:41:05.524
General Quarters! General Quarters!
All hands. man your battle stations!

538
00:41:07.190 --> 00:41:08.795
<i>BARKER [OVER RADIO]:
Bridge. TAO.</i>

539
00:41:08.810 --> 00:41:11.589
<i>SCUNK Alpha just energized
fire control radar.</i>

540
00:41:11.690 --> 00:41:15.146
- We're in their crosshairs.
<i>MAN 2 [ON RADIO]: Captain Tom Chandler?</i>

541
00:41:15.190 --> 00:41:19.053
This is Commander Chandler.
Identify yourself immediately.

542
00:41:19.670 --> 00:41:22.687
I'm sorry to have made
such a rude introduction...

543
00:41:23.510 --> 00:41:27.458
but I believe you have something
that I want.
